    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a balanced slate today, but the analytical ceiling is clearly defined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the team with a massive 83.29 efficiency score. He faces a favorable matchup against Buehler (4.56 xERA), and the combination of a high-park-factor environment and favorable wind conditions creates an elite situation for power output. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (71.85), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.38), **Kyle Tucker** (71.33), and **Andy Pages** (70.21) are our primary anchors today. Both **Jackson Merrill** and **Andy Pages** gain notable efficiency from a slow opposing delivery profile that enhances their SB floor\u2014a critical factor for the Waves given our obsession with speed\u2014while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leverages a strong platoon advantage to maintain his high tier of reliability.\n\nOn the bench, **Miguel Vargas** (45.42) was the final cut, falling just short of the marginal threshold required to displace players like **Dominic Smith** or **Wade Meckler**. While **Miguel Vargas** benefits from the favorable wind, his raw projected efficiency didn't quite stack up against the platoon-adjusted value offered by our current starters. We must exercise caution with **Liam Hicks**, who draws a difficult assignment against Skenes (2.99 xERA); despite a favorable order position, his score of 42.69 is buoyed almost exclusively by his lead-off role, making him a high-risk play today. Overall, the lineup is optimized to maximize plate appearances in favorable hitting conditions, with a heavy emphasis on mitigating the risks posed by elite arms like Skenes while capitalizing on the run-scoring opportunities provided by the secondary rotation arms we are facing.",
